{"source_family": "pallets/click", "revision": "08b803cf32ceb2ae6a772c62d5da42757a897d44", "facts": [{"id": "CK01", "written_source_meaning": "In the selected Context implementation, __init__ assigns self._meta = getattr(parent, \"meta\", {}). The meta property returns self._meta. For an ordinary Context parent using this getter, the child stores the parent meta mapping rather than a written copy; this does not establish sharing between unrelated root contexts.", "references": [{"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 411, "last_line": 411}, {"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 633, "last_line": 659}]}, {"id": "CK02", "written_source_meaning": "The constructor writes _depth=0. __enter__ increments _depth and calls push_context(self). __exit__ decrements _depth and, only when it is zero, calls _close_with_exception_info before the later pop_context call. Callee completion and overridden methods are not observed.", "references": [{"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 534, "last_line": 534}, {"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 576, "last_line": 579}, {"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 581, "last_line": 593}]}, {"id": "CK03", "written_source_meaning": "scope is decorated with contextmanager. When cleanup=False it increments depth before with self and decrements it in finally. On the ordinary normal path starting at depth0 without body mutation, the depth trace is0→1→2→1→0 and __exit__ skips its zero-depth cleanup branch. This does not prohibit explicit close calls or promise behavior of overrides or failing helpers.", "references": [{"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 595, "last_line": 631}]}, {"id": "CK04", "written_source_meaning": "call_on_close delegates to self._exit_stack.callback(f). _close_with_exception_info first calls the existing exit stack __exit__, then assigns a fresh ExitStack and returns the result. The reset is not in a finally block, so source does not guarantee the reset line is reached if the first call raises. Actual callback success and cross-thread/task isolation have not been observed.", "references": [{"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 704, "last_line": 714}, {"path": "src/click/core.py", "first_line": 723, "last_line": 739}]}], "uncertainty": {"callback_success_unverified": true, "thread_task_isolation_unverified": true, "click_runtime_execution_not_performed": true}, "questions": [{"id": "Q001", "question_en": "For the selected ordinary Context parent and getter, does a child reuse the parent meta mapping instead of making a copy?"}, {"id": "Q002", "question_en": "Which cleanup helper is called by __exit__ when its decremented _depth equals zero, and is it before the later pop_context call?"}, {"id": "Q003", "question_en": "Does cleanup=False force immediate automatic cleanup on the ordinary depth0 scope path?"}, {"id": "Q004", "question_en": "Do the examined source and unexecuted tests establish successful cleanup/reset and thread/task isolation under all runtime conditions?"}]}
